{
    "_doc": [
        "Who holds which mvs_* capability, and what each one AUTHORISES.",
        "",
        "The scope field is the point. WordPress capability names do not say whether they",
        "mean 'your own' or 'anyone's', and reading one the wrong way is a privilege",
        "escalation: Pro read edit_mvs_media as 'may edit any media' while Free grants it",
        "to every role including Subscriber and means 'your own', so any member could",
        "rewrite any other member's video chapters (2.5.1).",
        "",
        "scope:",
        "  own     - authorises the CALLER'S OWN object only. Never sufficient on its own",
        "            in a permission callback; pair it with an ownership comparison.",
        "  any     - authorises acting on anyone's object. The real site-wide authority.",
        "  site    - configuration and administration.",
        "  feature - 'may use this feature at all'. Fine as a bare entry gate, carries no",
        "            object authority.",
        "",
        "CapabilityMapTest asserts the live role grants still match `roles`, so widening a",
        "grant fails CI, and that no own-scope capability is used as a bare authority check",
        "outside `bare_check_allowlist`."
    ],
